   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "The function w is given by w(x) = (x^2 - 1)/(x - 1) for x < 1, w(x) = ax^2 + b for 1 <= x <= 3, and w(x) = 4x + 14 for x > 3, where a and b are constants. If w is continuous for all real x, what is the value of b?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": -1
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "As x approaches 1 from the left, (x^2 - 1)/(x - 1) = x + 1 tends to 2, and the middle branch gives a + b, so a + b = 2.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Equal",
            [
               "Add",
               "a",
               "b"
            ],
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "At x = 3 the middle branch gives 9a + b and the right branch gives 26, so 9a + b = 26.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Equal",
            [
               "Add",
               [
                  "Multiply",
                  9,
                  "a"
               ],
               "b"
            ],
            26
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Subtracting the first equation from the second gives 8a = 24, so a = 3.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Equal",
            "a",
            3
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Then b = 2 - 3 = -1.",
         "mathjson": -1
      }
   ],
